# shell: both
# The operation's own lifecycle is a fact: idle, then the job by
# caption, current leaf and count, then idle again.  The mid-flight
# claim is safe HERE because the in-process driver is turn-locked --
# the conducted lane, which races a real clock, claims only the
# endpoints (told.script).
wait 12
expect-operation idle
key a ctrl
wait 3
key c ctrl
wait 3
key v ctrl
note mid-flight the job speaks its count -- the one phrase every
note caption shares and idle never says
expect-operation of
expect-operation idle
quit
